    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle, we need to first understand what the mean value means. The mean value of a set of numbers is the sum of the numbers divided by the total count of numbers.\n\nIn this case, we have three interior angles of a triangle, and we want to find their mean value. Let's denote the measures of the three interior angles as A, B, and C.\n\nThe mean value of the three interior angles can be calculated using the formula:\n\nMean value = (A + B + C) / 3\n\nHowever, we know that the sum of the interior angles of any triangle is always 180 degrees. Therefore, we can substitute 180 for A + B + C in the formula:\n\nMean value = 180 / 3\n\nMean value = 60\n\nSo, the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle is 60 degrees.",
